WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.521 --> 00:00:06.590
Narrator: That roar belongs
to one of the most iconic

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:09.610
movie monsters of all time:

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.120
Godzilla.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.810
Since his debut in 1954,

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.980
the King of Monsters has
rampaged across Tokyo,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.990
New York City, and Osaka

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.300
to name a few.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.200
And over the years, he's gotten bigger,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.875
and bigger,

00:00:24.875 --> 00:00:26.290
and bigger.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.915
The latest Godzilla is a record

00:00:28.915 --> 00:00:32.120
119 meters tall,

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:36.370
about six times taller than
the tallest animal in history.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.540
And to be fair,

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.160
it's a fantasy film, not
a nature documentary.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.040
But just how fantastical
is a 36-story-tall

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.459
lizard-dinosaur creature who breathes

00:00:46.459 --> 00:00:49.020
beams of atomic energy?

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.540
Well, energy beams aside,

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.930
Godzilla is actually even more unrealistic

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.013
than you might think.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.720
Now, Earth is no stranger
to enormous animals.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.150
Just look at the largest dinosaur,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.890
the titanosaurs,

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.650
or today's blue whales,

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.690
which reach up to 30 meters long

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.810
and can weigh 200 tons.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.370
Compared to them,

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:20.340
Godzilla doesn't seem
that impossible, right?

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.760
- These critters are
massive on a scale that's

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.817
just totally impossible.

00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:26.650
I mean,

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:30.210
assuming, at least, they're
made of anything even remotely

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:31.788
like what we're made out of

00:01:31.788 --> 00:01:33.760
and follow any of the roles of biology,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.830
they are completely impossible.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.440
Narrator: That's
paleontologist Mike Habib.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.960
He's an expert in giant reptiles

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.910
and also helps design
fantastical creatures

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.580
for TV and film.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.080
And according to him,

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.630
a creature like Godzilla
could never exist in real life

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.560
for multiple reasons.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:57.170
First, he would be brain-dead
long before he ever

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:58.560
reached a city

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.300
because his heart simply isn't
large and powerful enough

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.170
to pump blood to his head.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.080
- His heart would have
to be thousands of tons

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.170
and fill most of his chest.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:10.740
You'd have to have vessels that you could

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.233
drive a car through,

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:18.950
and he would need the energy
consumption of a small

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.760
power plant, probably, every
minute in order to run it.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.140
Of course, he's nuclear-powered,

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.750
so maybe he has the energy to spare.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:25.860
Narrator: In reality,

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.900
large animals like titanosaurs

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.430
got around this by walking
on all fours with their heads

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.950
held out in front them,

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.460
not held up high.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.380
That way, they don't have to pump blood

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.260
against gravity as far.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.240
But even if Godzilla did crawl
across cities on all fours,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.480
he'd have another problem:

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.520
movement.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.440
You see, whenever you
lift your leg or arm,

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:51.810
it's because your brain fires
signals to the nerves in your

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.490
leg and arm muscles.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.990
The fastest of these signals travel around

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:58.140
100 meters per second,

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:02.780
so the message from brain to
leg is virtually instantaneous.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.330
Not for Godzilla though.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.940
It would take more than a full
second for nerve signals to

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.750
travel the length of his body.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:13.490
Now, a second still sounds pretty quick,

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.860
but in reality...

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.100
Mike Habib: His nerve-conduction speed

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.390
becomes so slow that he can't move.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:20.230
Takes forever to do anything.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:22.390
Narrator: Now, Godzilla does look pretty

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.400
sluggish in the films,

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.493
but it turns out, in reality,
it would look more like this.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.220
But even if Godzilla
could move super fast,

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.420
he wouldn't have time to fight enemies

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:37.090
or demolish buildings

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:40.160
because he'd be too busy sunbathing.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.660
All animals need a way to
regulate body temperature.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.660
Reptiles and other
cold-blooded animals stay warm

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.610
by basking in the sun.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:50.230
But in Godzilla's case,

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.650
heat from the sun would have
to travel through meters upon

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.760
meters of tissue to penetrate his hide

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.940
and reach his internal organs.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:01.610
So to stay warm, he'd have
to spend hundreds of hours

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.680
straight sunbathing.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.570
But what if Godzilla
were more like a mammal?

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:07.650
Like us?

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.880
He wouldn't need to rely on the sun

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:14.050
since we warm-blooded creatures
produce our own body heat.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.640
But unfortunately,

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.980
that would cause yet another problem.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:18.813
- But then he's so big,

00:04:18.813 --> 00:04:21.110
he probably cooks himself.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.840
His core temperature hits 300 degrees.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:25.790
Narrator: Yikes.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:30.060
And even if he somehow got
around all these problems,

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:33.650
his skeleton would still
collapse under its own weight.

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:38.570
Now, Mike says he's a
whopping 90,000 metric tons,

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:41.950
and that skeleton's just
not strong enough to support

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:45.860
90,000 metric tons of, well, anything.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:47.027
- Yeah, he would just crumple.

00:04:47.027 --> 00:04:47.860
Yeah.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:48.730
He'd just collapse.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:52.080
He'd be a very large pile of meat.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.530
Narrator: Not a very intimidating picture.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:55.370
In the end,

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.040
Mike says Godzilla could only
be about half as tall as he

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.700
was in the original film

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.320
before his poor heart would give out.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.500
But just because Godzilla's
body is unrealistic

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.750
doesn't mean it's bad.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.430
In fact, he's perfect for the role.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:14.630
He's tall enough to stalk
past city skyscrapers,

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:17.523
which give us iconic scenes like this.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:24.174
Mike: Just straight-up magic in the 
modern world setting

00:05:24.174 --> 00:05:27.344
and just go and enjoy it
as such.

